BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:164299@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20260709T094608Z
DTSTART:20260701T125000Z
SUMMARY:The Q2 2026 Critical Path Schedule (CPS) update for non-commercial resources is now due
DESCRIPTION:Pursuant to the ISO New England Inc. Transmission\, Markets\, and Services Tariff Section III.13.3\, the Q2 2026 CPS update is now due for those non-commercial resources that either cleared in a Forward Capacity Auction or requested monitoring of their CPS. Please submit the update under the Monitored CPS tab in the Forward Capacity Tracking System (FCTS) for all applicable Capacity Commitment Periods as appropriate. The update should be submitted by the end of Wednesday\, July 8\, 2026 (by 23:59).\n\nPursuant to Section III.13.3.2.2 of the ISO New England Inc. Transmission\, Markets\, and Services Tariff\, " for each critical path schedule milestone achieved since the submission of the previous critical path schedule report\, the Project Sponsor must include in the critical path schedule report documentation demonstrating that the milestone has been achieved by the date indicated".  This section of the ISO New England Inc. Transmission\, Markets\, and Services Tariff also provides detailed examples of the type of documentation that can be included to demonstrate completion of each milestone.\n\nReview the Critical Path Schedule Report Training presentation here for guidance on submitting the CPS report in FCTS.\n\nIf you experience any technical issues while submitting the report or if you have any questions regarding this message\, please contact the Participant Support and Solutions Team by submitting a case via Ask ISO\, emailing AskISO@iso-ne.com\, or by phone at (413) 540-4220.\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=164299
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=164299
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:160148@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20260709T094608Z
DTSTART:20260701T133000Z
DTEND:20260701T203000Z
SUMMARY:NEPOOL Power Supply Planning Committee Meeting
LOCATION:WebEx
DESCRIPTION:NEPOOL meetings\, while not public\, are open to all NEPOOL Participants\, their authorized representatives and\, except as otherwise limited for discussions in executive session\, consumer advocates\, federal and state officials and guests whose attendance has been cleared with the Committee Chair. All those in attendance or participating\, either in person or by phone\, are required to identify themselves and their affiliation at the meeting. Official records and minutes of meetings are posted publicly. No statements made in NEPOOL meetings are to be quoted or published publicly.\n\nWebEx Meeting Calendar\n\nNote: If you wish to dial in via telephone\, please reach out to Peter Asarese for connection details prior to the meeting start date.\n\nFor all other meeting-related inquiries\, please contact the respective committee secretary listed below.\n\nAdd to My Calendar\nContact: Jillian Macura (jmacura@iso-ne.com)\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=160148
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=160148
END:VEVENT
